# Copy to web/.env (git-ignored) and fill in. Read only by the Next.js server (and the npm scripts below), never
# sent to the browser: nothing here has a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, and none may. On Vercel, set these in the project's
# Environment Variables instead.
#
# No database or Claude key needed to work on the UI: `npm run dev:local` serves the snapshot JSON file with the
# code ranker (DATA_SOURCE=json SNAPSHOT_ID=2026-10-27 RANKER_MODE=baseline), no model calls.
#
# Tests. Settings can come from this file or the shell (a variable already set in the shell wins).
#   npm test                   unit tests with fakes; no database, no model calls. Run on every change.
#   npm run test:integration   real API + real Postgres (read-only, staged snapshot 2026-10-27, code ranker,
#                              free). Needs DATABASE_URL; skips without it.
#   RUN_PAID_TESTS=1 npm run test:e2e:claude
#                              one real search through the Claude Ranker + Reviewer. COSTS MONEY (at most 6 model
#                              calls). Needs DATABASE_URL, Anthropic credentials and RUN_PAID_TESTS=1; skips otherwise.

# Supabase > Connect. On Vercel (serverless) use the Transaction pooler (port 6543); locally either pooler works.
# Use the pooler host, not db.<ref>.supabase.co, which is IPv6-only.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.ofjwdioysmzfeiqlfrkl:<db-password>@aws-0-us-east-1.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres
# TLS to the database: require (default: encrypted) | verify (encrypted + certificate checked against
# DATABASE_SSL_CA, the CA file from Supabase > Database Settings > SSL Configuration) | off (local Postgres only).
# Don't put sslmode in DATABASE_URL; it overrides this setting.
# DATABASE_SSL=require
# DATABASE_SSL_CA=

# Ranker and Reviewer. Or run `ant auth login` and leave this unset.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# CLAUDE_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5

# ---- Results API (server/api). Every setting below is optional; the value shown is the default. ----
# ranker_reviewer | ranker_only | baseline (code ranker, no model calls, no credentials needed)
# RANKER_MODE=ranker_reviewer
# Serve this snapshot instead of the published one. Local development only.
# SNAPSHOT_ID=
# postgres (DATABASE_URL) | json (data/snapshots/<SNAPSHOT_ID>/records.json; no database; needs SNAPSHOT_ID).
# The JSON file lives outside web/ and is not bundled into a Vercel deployment: use postgres there.
# DATA_SOURCE=postgres
# Per-day JSONL trace directory. Unset: the repo's traces/ (git-ignored), or off on Vercel (read-only filesystem).
# Set to empty to turn tracing off.
# TRACE_DIR=

# Per-visitor rate limits key on a signed visitor cookie (HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, 30 days; src/proxy.ts and
# server/api/visitor.ts), so classmates on one network each get their own limit. This secret signs it: at least 32
# characters, generate with `openssl rand -hex 32`, keep it out of git, and set a different one per environment
# (Vercel: Preview and Production). Changing it just re-issues everyone a cookie. Unset or shorter than 32: no
# cookie, every visitor is keyed by their address as below (logged once; on Vercel as a WARNING), never an error.
# VISITOR_COOKIE_SECRET=
# Visitors without a valid cookie, and the per-address ceiling over all cookie visitors (4x each limit below, so a
# pile of cookies from one address can't multiply its allowance), use the visitor's address: the last entry of
# X-Forwarded-For, which is read only on Vercel or when TRUST_FORWARDED_FOR=1 (set it only behind a proxy that
# sets that header, e.g. nginx with $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for). Exposed directly, a visitor could write their own
# and pick a fresh limit per request. Unset (and not on Vercel): every address-keyed visitor shares one limit.
# TRUST_FORWARDED_FOR=

# Cost controls. All are per server process and reset on restart. On Vercel each serverless instance keeps its own
# counters and cache, so the effective limits across the deployment are looser than these numbers.
# Model-backed runs one visitor (cookie, else address; IPv6: per /64) may start per minute. A search counts one per type that is not
# cached, charged all at once. Cache hits don't count. At least 5.
# RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE=10
# Search and opportunities requests one visitor (cookie, else address; IPv6: per /64) may make per minute, in every mode, cached or not,
# budget left or not: bounds server and database work. One search counts once, however many types it asks for.
# SEARCH_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE=30
# Model-backed runs at once; up to MAX_QUEUED_RUNS more wait up to QUEUE_WAIT_MS. Then a search serves that type
# from the code ranker (Tier 2, not fully checked) instead.
# MAX_CONCURRENT_RUNS=2
# MAX_QUEUED_RUNS=8
# QUEUE_WAIT_MS=10000
# Model calls (each Ranker or Reviewer call) per local day. When used up, searches get Tier 2 from the code ranker.
# DAILY_MODEL_CALLS=300
# A search starts no new model call after this and returns the best tier reached (Tier 2).
# REQUEST_DEADLINE_MS=90000
# Timeout for one model call.
# MODEL_CALL_TIMEOUT_MS=60000
# Cached results (bounded). Identical searches on the same day and snapshot make no model calls.
# CACHE_MAX_ENTRIES=500
